-- title:
--   Frobenius-type endomorphisms of the Drinfeld function field are integral
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $k$ a field, and let $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,k$ be the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`; assume this quotient is an integral domain, and write $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q k` for its fraction field, a $k$-algebra. Let $\varphi : F \to F$ be a $k$-algebra homomorphism, let $n$ be a natural number, and denote by $x$ and $y$ the images in $F$ of the distinguished elements `x q k` and `y q k` of the coordinate ring under the canonical map to the fraction field. Suppose $\varphi(x) = x^{q^n}$ and $\varphi(y) = y^{q^n}$. Then the underlying ring homomorphism of $\varphi$ is integral in the sense of `RingHom.IsIntegral`: every element of $F$ satisfies a monic polynomial all of whose coefficients lie in the image $\varphi(F)$.
--
--   This is the integrality of a Frobenius-type $k$-endomorphism of the function field of the Drinfeld curve, reflecting the fact that such an endomorphism makes $F$ a finite extension of its image. It supplies the integrality hypothesis under which places of the function field may be pulled back along the endomorphism, and is used in the computations of [`DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.finrank_eigenspace_rootsOfUnity_rationalTateModule_eq) and [`DrinfeldCurve.intertwiningMap_twist_eq_zero_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.intertwiningMap_twist_eq_zero_of_isCuspidalOfType_of_isAlgClosed).
